xnu 0131: single-frame bit-bang, a MISO float test and the ldoc2 vote

The first bit-bang read returned zeros in both framings. Two things changed:
the command/address and the data now share one CS frame (the part latches
the address and drives MISO with CS still low), and the clock is slower
(~600 kHz). Before reading, MISO is sampled with a pull-up and with a
pull-down: a floating pad means nothing drives the part's IO, which for a
powered and de-reset part means its IOVDD rail is off.

That rail is pm8350c_l2, an RPMh VRM: read its address from the AOP command
DB (0x80860000, key "ldoc2") and send voltage 1800 mV and enable through the
first ACTIVE TCS of apps_rsc drv-2 (0x17a20000, TCS block +0xd00, rpmh-rsc
3.0 layout), then sample MISO again.

